Z||000004||Dale||09-21-1999||03:25 AM||||Pretender,<BR>What kind of tires did you get.  I am finding that once you get to that size it's hard to run more than 32psi unless your camber is set to "0".  You start wearing the insides of the tire.  I learned that the hard way.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pretender||09-21-1999||03:39 AM||||i got them from sears (faulkin's*spelling?*) i'm running 215/50/15's in the front and the 225's in the rear, i also learned my leson the hard way last time. What ever jiffy lube put in them i guess, well SCREW JIFFY LUBE*another story*, so you reccomend about 32psi? i doubt that my camber is set to 0 because the peps at sears probably set it back to stock stuff when they did the 4 wheel alignment. it says on the recipt that they put 35 in the front but there is no mention about the rear on the paperwork.:0(||||reg||10
